{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I will come down.</b> This teaches that this day was as beloved before the Holy One, blessed be He, as the day of the giving of the Torah, as it is said: ״כי ביום השלישי ירד ה' על הר סיני״." "<b>And I will take some of the spirit that is upon you.</b> A parable: a king who had a fine orchard and hired a guard to watch it. After some days the guard said to him: I cannot watch it all alone; rather, bring others to watch it with me. The king said to him: To you I gave the orchard to watch, and all the wages for guarding it I gave to you. And now you say to bring others? As you live, I will not give them wages for guarding from my own — rather, from the wages I set for you. Thus the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: To you I gave spirit and knowledge to sustain My children, and I was not seeking others, and you said: ״לא אוכל לבדי״. As you live, they shall not take from My own — but ״ואצלתי מן הרוח אשר עליך״. And even so, Moses lacked nothing. Know this, for after forty years the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: ״קח את יהושע ונתת מהודך עליו״ — that he lacked nothing from him. Like a lamp that was burning and they lit from it several lamps, and the light of its own burning lacked nothing."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:11.670074008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}